==Swedish==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|sv}} {{term|þorp|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|sv}} {{m|gem-pro|*þurpą}}, whence also with German {{term|Dorf|lang=de}} and Dutch {{term|dorp|lang=nl}}.

===Noun===
{{sv-noun|n}}

# {{context|before 16th century|lang=sv}} A solitary [[farm]], distant from other settlements
# {{context|16th century|lang=sv}} ''Officially defined'' as a very small farm
# {{context|17th century to early 20th century|lang=sv}} A small farm, [[rent]]ed from a larger [[land owner]], where the rent was payed through work on the owner's land ([[dagsverken]])
# {{context|after the 1940's|lang=sv}} A small [[cottage]] in the [[countryside]]

